# Every skill embeds a bash block that Claude Code lifts out of SKILL.md and runs
# verbatim. A CRLF checkout puts a carriage return at the end of every line of that
# block, and bash answers with `$'\r': command not found` before anything runs. Git
# for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, so without this file the plugin
# breaks on exactly the machines least likely to diagnose it.
* text=auto eol=lf
